## Text-to-Speech API Reference

> Generate speech audio from text using the FPT.AI-VITs model. Supports multiple output formats including `.mp3`, `.wav`, and `.caf` (iOS).


### Endpoint

```
POST https://mkp-api.fptcloud.com/v1/audio/speech
```



### Request

#### Headers

| Header | Value |
|---|---|
| `Authorization` | `Bearer <your-api-key>` |
| `Content-Type` | `application/json` |

#### Body Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `model` | `string` | **required** | Model name. Use `FPT.AI-VITs`. |
| `input` | `string` | **required** | The text to synthesize. |
| `voice` | `string` | `std_leminh` | Voice ID to use. See [Available Voices](#available-voices). |
| `response_type` | `string` | `audio` | Output delivery format. One of `audio`, `base64`, or `zip`. |
| `response_format` | `string \| string[]` | `wav` | Audio format(s). One of or a list of `mp3`, `wav`, `caf`. See [Response Format Rules](#response-format-rules). |
| `speed` | `float` | `1` | Speech speed multiplier. |
| `sample_rate` | `integer` | `22050` | Audio sample rate in Hz. |


### Response Format Rules

The allowed values for `response_format` depend on the chosen `response_type`:

- **`response_type: "audio"`** — Returns a single audio file directly. `response_format` must be a single string or a list with exactly one element.
  ```json
  "response_format": "mp3"
  // or
  "response_format": ["mp3"]
  ```

- **`response_type: "base64"`** — Returns audio encoded in Base64. Supports multiple formats simultaneously.
  ```json
  "response_format": ["mp3", "caf", "wav"]
  ```

- **`response_type: "zip"`** — Returns a ZIP archive containing all requested audio files. Supports multiple formats simultaneously.
  ```json
  "response_format": ["mp3", "caf", "wav"]
  ```



### Examples

#### Single audio file (default)

```bash
curl --request POST \
  --url https://mkp-api.fptcloud.com/v1/audio/speech \
  --header 'Authorization: Bearer <your-api-key>' \
  --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  --data '{
    "model": "FPT.AI-VITs",
    "input": "Xin chào, đây là bài kiểm tra.",
    "voice": "banmai",
    "response_type": "audio",
    "response_format": "mp3",
    "speed": 1,
    "sample_rate": 22050
  }'
```

#### Multiple formats as Base64

Returns a JSON object with each requested format encoded in Base64 — suitable for applications that need both Android (`.mp3`) and iOS (`.caf`) outputs in a single request.

```bash
curl --request POST \
  --url https://mkp-api.fptcloud.com/v1/audio/speech \
  --header 'Authorization: Bearer <your-api-key>' \
  --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  --data '{
    "model": "FPT.AI-VITs",
    "input": "Xin chào, đây là bài kiểm tra.",
    "voice": "banmai",
    "response_type": "base64",
    "response_format": ["mp3", "caf", "wav"],
    "speed": 1,
    "sample_rate": 22050
  }'
```

#### Multiple formats as ZIP

```bash
curl --request POST \
  --url https://mkp-api.fptcloud.com/v1/audio/speech \
  --header 'Authorization: Bearer <your-api-key>' \
  --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  --data '{
    "model": "FPT.AI-VITs",
    "input": "Xin chào, đây là bài kiểm tra.",
    "voice": "banmai",
    "response_type": "zip",
    "response_format": ["mp3", "caf"],
    "speed": 1,
    "sample_rate": 22050
  }'
```



### Available Voices

> Contact the FPT.AI Voice team for the full and up-to-date list of available voice IDs.



### Notes

- The staging environment is available at `https://mkp-api-stg.fptcloud.net` for testing.
- To serve both **Android** (`.mp3`) and **iOS** (`.caf`) clients, use `response_type: "base64"` or `"zip"` with `response_format: ["mp3", "caf"]`.
